## 4. Building Blocks Reference

### 4.1 Score Ring (SVG)

```html
<div class="score-ring">
  <svg width="100" height="100">
    <circle class="bg" cx="50" cy="50" r="42"
      fill="none" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,.08)" stroke-width="6"/>
    <circle class="progress" cx="50" cy="50" r="42"
      fill="none" stroke="var(--severity-pass)" stroke-width="6"
      stroke-dasharray="264"
      stroke-dashoffset="53"  <!-- 264 - (264 * percentage) -->
      stroke-linecap="round"
      style="transform:rotate(-90deg);transform-origin:center"/>
  </svg>
  <span class="value">80%</span>
</div>
```

**Công thức**: `stroke-dashoffset = circumference - (circumference × percentage)`
- `circumference = 2 × π × r = 2 × 3.14159 × 42 ≈ 264`
- 80% → `264 - (264 × 0.80) = 264 - 211.2 ≈ 53`

### 4.2 Severity Badge

```html
<span class="badge critical">Critical</span>
<span class="badge major">Major</span>
<span class="badge minor">Minor</span>
<span class="badge pass">Pass</span>
```

```css
.badge {
  display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .35rem;
  padding: .2rem .65rem; border-radius: 20px;
  font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 600;
  text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .03em;
}
.badge.critical { background: rgba(239,68,68,.15); color: #fca5a5; }
.badge.major    { background: rgba(249,115,22,.15); color: #fdba74; }
.badge.minor    { background: rgba(234,179,8,.15);  color: #fde047; }
.badge.pass     { background: rgba(34,197,94,.15);  color: #86efac; }
```

### 4.3 Progressive Disclosure (Native HTML)

```html
<details>
  <summary>Xem đề xuất & DDL reference →</summary>
  <div class="detail-content">
    <strong>Đề xuất:</strong> ...
    <strong>DDL:</strong> ...
    <strong>UX Law:</strong> ...
  </div>
</details>
```

Zero JS, fully accessible, print-friendly. Executives xem summary, designers expand detail.

### 4.4 Scroll Progress Bar

```html
<div class="scroll-progress"><div class="bar" id="progressBar"></div></div>
```

```css
.scroll-progress {
  position: fixed; top: 56px; left: 0; right: 0;
  height: 3px; z-index: 999;
  background: rgba(255,255,255,.05);
}
.scroll-progress .bar {
  height: 100%;
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--accent-purple), var(--accent-gold));
  width: 0%;
}
```

```js
window.addEventListener('scroll', () => {
  const h = document.documentElement.scrollHeight - window.innerHeight;
  const pct = h > 0 ? (window.scrollY / h) * 100 : 0;
  document.getElementById('progressBar').style.width = pct + '%';
});
```

### 4.5 Scroll-Reveal Animation

```js
const observer = new IntersectionObserver(entries => {
  entries.forEach(e => { if (e.isIntersecting) e.target.classList.add('visible'); });
}, { threshold: 0.12 });
document.querySelectorAll('.scroll-section').forEach(s => observer.observe(s));
```

```css
.scroll-section {
  opacity: 0; transform: translateY(40px);
  transition: opacity 0.7s ease, transform 0.7s ease;
}
.scroll-section.visible { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
```

### 4.6 Animated Counter

```js
function animateCounter(element, target, duration = 1200) {
  let start = null;
  const step = (timestamp) => {
    if (!start) start = timestamp;
    const progress = Math.min((timestamp - start) / duration, 1);
    element.textContent = Math.floor(progress * target);
    if (progress < 1) requestAnimationFrame(step);
  };
  requestAnimationFrame(step);
}
```

### 4.7 Card Filter (JS)

```js
const findings = [ /* array of finding objects */ ];

function renderCards(filter) {
  const filtered = filter === 'all' ? findings :
    findings.filter(f => f.sev === filter || f.screen === filter);
  
  grid.innerHTML = filtered.map(f => `
    <div class="audit-card explorer-card">
      <div class="card-header">
        <span class="card-id">${f.id}</span>
        <span class="badge ${f.sev}">${f.sev}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="card-body">
        <h4>${f.title}</h4>
        <p>${f.desc}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card-footer">
        ${f.tags.map(t => `<span class="card-tag">${t}</span>`).join('')}
      </div>
    </div>
  `).join('');
}
```

